 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Capacity Constraint:** If a single mesh-cell's global ray-segment count $R_m$ exceeds $C_{max}$, the load balance criterion is violated. The sources do not specify a fallback for this degenerate case [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Tie Breaking:** The sources do not specify tie-breaking rules for $\arg\max$ or $\arg\min$ operations. Implementers should choose a deterministic rule (e.g., lowest processor ID) [G].
-*   **Pre-computation Dependency:** The algorithm assumes global data is available. Failure to correctly perform the global-sum and global-max steps will result in incorrect assignments [S1, unofficial].
